 "notes": "Closed exclusion region from Fig. 1 (figs/g_agg_constraints.pdf) of the e-print: union of the paper's new irreducible freeze-in constraints on the photophilic axion (T_RH = 5 MeV) from X-ray searches (mustard), the cosmic X-ray/gamma-ray background CRB (lime), and CMB anisotropies (velvet). Pre-existing astrophysical bounds (HB stars, SN1987A, solar basin) and the SD/BBN regions taken from other papers are excluded. Region extracted from the vector PDF by color-selecting the filled regions at 300 dpi (dashed/dotted future-sensitivity and Simons-Array projection curves removed); axes calibrated from tick marks and verified against the abstract's quoted value g_agamma < 8.1e-14 GeV^-1 at m_a = 10 keV (extraction gives 8.3e-14). The bound is two-sided (large couplings escape because the axion decays early), so the points trace a closed loop: starting at minimum mass (~130 eV), along the lower (strong-coupling-reach) boundary to the tip at ~30 MeV, then back along the upper boundary; masses converted keV -> eV. Confidence level not explicitly stated in the paper; 0.95 assumed (underlying X-ray limits are 95% CL). No local DM density dependence (cosmological abundance bound).",
